ummary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Discussed in https://github.com/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/discussions/8691\r\n\r\nWe need to set up ``__allow_unmapped__`` as a first class way to have declarative types that are incorrect to be ignored, for 1.4 compatibility.\r\n\r\nright now it fails for this case:\r\n\r\n```py\r\nfrom __future__ import annotations\r\n\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import create_engine\r\nfrom sqlalchemy import ForeignKey\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import DeclarativeBase\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import Mapped\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import mapped_column\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import relationship\r\nfrom sqlalchemy.orm import Session\r\n\r\n\r\nclass Base(DeclarativeBase):\r\n    pass\r\n    __allow_unmapped__ = True\r\n\r\n\r\nclass A(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"a\"\r\n\r\n    id: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(primary_key=True)\r\n    data: Mapped[str]\r\n    bs: list[B] = relationship(\"B\")\r\n\r\n\r\nclass B(Base):\r\n    __tablename__ = \"b\"\r\n    id: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(primary_key=True)\r\n    a_id: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(ForeignKey(\"a.id\"))\r\n    data: Mapped[str]\r\n\r\n\r\ne = create_engine(\"sqlite://\", echo=True)\r\nBase.metadata.create_all(e)\r\n\r\ns = Session(e)\r\n\r\ns.add(A(bs=[B()]))\r\ns.commit()\r\n```\r\n\r\nbecause:\r\n\r\n```\r\nWhen initializing mapper Mapper[A(a)], expression \"relationship('list[B]')\" seems to be using a generic class as the argument to relationship(); please state the generic argument using an annotation, e.g. \"bs: Mapped[list['B']] = relationship()\"\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhat it should do is completely not use that annotation that was detected as \"wrong\".\r\n\r\nalso the error message raised for the non-evaluable annotation is very confusing and im not sure what I has in mind when I wrote that.   so let's make something less ambiguous.","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/8692/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sqlalchemy/issues/8692/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}